  "QRF_interpretation": [
    "QRF lowers mean pinball loss versus F in2/8 cells and has higher loss in6/8. Its favorable FXH6W2880 comparison is -4.480033534527601%, DMp0.12644858102549553; favorable TreasuryH6W52 is -6.829604681280947%, DMp0.3173500876102757. Neither is significant by the recorded working-reference DM test, and both have Holm1.0.",
    "QRF lowers loss versus original QR in5/8 cells and raises it in3/8. Only two QRF-minus-QR slots have original48-slot Holm p<.05: FXH6W2880 has higher loss(+12.068917392039936%, Holm0.0001310282134163148); TreasuryH6W52 has lower loss(-49.18564651031964%, Holm0.013132949227230713). These opposing directions preclude a universal winner claim.",
    "TreasuryH6W260 QRF-minus-QR is favorable by -29.570262031257382%, with unadjusted DMp0.0012052714837964584, but its original48-slot Holm p0.05062140231945125 exceeds .05. A doubled-bandwidth result does not replace the frozen primary-bandwidth adjustment.",
    "No QRF-minus-F slot has Holm p<.05. Lack of rejection is not equivalence, lack of feature value, or proof the family cannot outperform F.",
    "These p values are read from saved results, not newly recomputed here. DM/HAC and HLN remain approximate under shared training, overlapping targets, possible long dependence, small Treasury sample and post-inspection procedure selection. Holm only adjusts its defined48slots assuming valid component p values; it does not validate that assumption or all research choices."
  ],
